            <ArticleTitle>A case of rifampicin induced pseudomembraneous colitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1391-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case pf pseudomembranous colitis that developed in a patient with tuberculous abdominal lymphadenopathy during treatment with rifampicin. The patient had delayed presentation (3 months) after the start of rifampicin. She had one relapse after 2 months that was successfully treated, and she finished her antituberculosis therapy without any further relapses. Awareness of this serious complication of rifampicin therapy should be encountered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
